{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Scholarship Application Overview",
  "subtitle": "A snapshot of applicant status, academic performance, and regional distribution.",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Applicants",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Approved Rate",
    "sql": "SELECT (COUNT(CASE WHEN \"Status\" = 'Approved' THEN 1 END) * 100.0 / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0)) AS pct FROM \"scholarship_applicants\"",
    "unit": "%"
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Applicants by Status",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Status\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "Status",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Average Marks by Taluka",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Taluka\", AVG(\"Marks %\") AS avg_marks FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Marks %\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
    "x": "Taluka",
    "y": [
     "avg_marks"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Average Family Income by Category",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Category\", AVG(\"Family Income\") AS avg_income FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" WHERE \"Family Income\" IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "Category",
    "y": [
     "avg_income"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top 10 Talukas by Applicant Count",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Taluka\", COUNT(*) AS total_applicants, ROUND(AVG(\"Marks %\"), 2) AS avg_marks FROM \"scholarship_applicants\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard currently tracks {{p1}} total scholarship applications. The approval rate stands at {{p2}}%, indicating the proportion of applicants who have successfully cleared the initial review stage.\n\nIn terms of academic performance, the taluka with the highest average marks is {{p4}}, while the category with the highest average family income is {{p5}}. These metrics help identify regions and demographic groups that may require different support strategies.\n\nFor a detailed breakdown, refer to the table showing the top 10 talukas by applicant volume. The leading region is {{p6}}, which accounts for a significant portion of the total applications."
 },
